    "abstract": "2022, only 68.9% of world's population consumed daily food allowance, an insufficient amount of dietary energy to ensure maintenance of a normal, active and healthy life (Bakhmat et al., 2023).Another extremely important problem on a global scale is climate change, which has been observed for several decades.It is caused mainly by anthropogenic human activity, which leads to an increase in content of carbon dioxide in atmosphere.Modern climate change is manifested primarily in the steady increase in average annual and seasonal air temperatures, as well as in significant spatial and temporal unevenness of precipitation both within individual regions and on a global scale",
    "field": "Fodder production and carbon sequestration",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge of developing agricultural technologies that can simultaneously increase fodder production to combat food insecurity and enhance carbon sequestration to mitigate climate change, which are often conflicting goals in conventional farming.",
    "method": "This paper proposes an agricultural system of growing winter intermediate rye followed by post-harvest soybeans to simultaneously increase fodder production and enhance carbon sequestration on the same arable land within a year.",
    "task": "The task is to assess the productivity and carbon sequestration potential of using winter intermediate fodder crops in a double-cropping system with post-harvest soybeans in the Western Forest-Steppe of Ukraine.",
